        "raw": "<p>i *may* have a question that I&#39;m pretty sure of the answer to, but just to make sure here, cause it was such a weird circumstance of events.</p><p>so we had Haka, Crono Ranger, and Nightmist fighting La Capitan in the Time Cataclysm. first several rounds went as per the usual, shenangians ensued, and long story short we were in a tough spot with Crono-Ranger at 3 HP left with an armory in front of him, Haka with his Club of Smashiness and Stick of Beatings(I forget what they&#39;re actually called, but it&#39;s the only equipment he has[and yes, this is important to the question]) and Savage Mana, with Nightmist having her nice compliment of amazing healing every round. La Capitan had a nice array of her grunt people out, who were all nicely damaged and primed for being sucked under Savage Mana, but i couldn&#39;t get at all of them without a Rampage, which of course would kill off Chrono Ranger. as a group, we had all decided it was the best option, since he was going to get knocked out regardless of what any of us did. As Haka, i was the last player to go, so this was a massive decision.</p><p>My question is this: since RAMPAGE knocked out Chrono-Ranger, thereby &quot;destroying&quot; him, would he get pulled into Savage Mana as well as any others that got destroyed by that same card?</p>",
